<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kiribati</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kiribati is an island republic in the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pacific-ocean">Pacific Ocean</a>, made up of 33 atolls and reef islands in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humphrey-gilbert">Gilbert</a>, Phoenix and Line groups, with its capital at South Tarawa. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gilbert-islands">Gilbert Islands</a> became a British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> in 1892 and later part of the Gilbert and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ellice-islands">Ellice Islands</a> colony, and Tarawa saw a fierce battle in 1943. It became independent in 1979, its name being the local form of 'Gilberts'.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kiribati.jpg" alt="Kiribati" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hanzlan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Kiribati.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
